+# DOT timing notes named in the FAA chronology recipient's interview
+
+Reviewed November 9, 2026 Eastern. B129 / PD01 / PD07. The April 2004 interview memorandum for the Secretary of Transportation's chief of staff names a set of staff timing notes. The separate handwritten file preserves a corresponding lead. The earlier FAA visit memo says a chronology was in preparation for the chief of staff. The documents leave open what was prepared, sent or retained.
+
+| Source and locator | Observation |
+| --- | --- |
+| FAA Operations Center visit memorandum, NARA 00244, p. 1 lines 8–12, 18–22 | The archived opening memo dates the visit **6/4/2003**. It reports FAA was preparing a chronology of events and actions for Secretary Mineta's chief of staff, John Flaherty. The working-copy date fields and their conflicts are preserved in the prior comparison. |
+| Team 8 interview memorandum, item 819, p. 1 lines 3–12 and p. 5 lines 23–26 | Dated **April 2004**. The memo says Flaherty did not keep notes from the day. After a question about whether a timeline was constructed, it records **“No, there wasn't a timeline for DOT.”** It names **Geenie Norris** as taking timing notes and attributes the description **“contradictory and in dribs and drabs”** to Flaherty. P. 3 lines 3–4 uses the same spelling elsewhere in the memo. |
+| Dana Hyde file, p. 1 line 2 and p. 2 | P. 1 is headed **Potential Questions for John Flaherty**. P. 2 continues the numbered list. These pages supply question prompts. |
+| Same Hyde file, p. 6 lower block and p. 7 middle block | The handwriting on p. 6 appears to read **“Jeannie Norris took notes on time”**, with a final stroke that may be a question mark. The first-name reading is tentative. P. 7 reads **“Can't help w/ Timeline”** Those are note fragments. No original DOT timing sheet accompanies them in these passages. |
+
+The typed and handwritten accounts overlap on the timing-note lead and other interview topics. The files represent related Commission interview material. Preserve **Geenie** and the tentative **Jeannie** reading together. The handwriting does not establish an alternate official spelling, an independent witness or a second set of notes.
+
+The **FAA chronology under preparation** and **no timeline for DOT** statements remain separately attributed. Their scopes and dates differ. The record leaves open whether the two statements refer to the same intended chronology, or whether the June work reached the recipient. The memo's attribution of timing notes supplies a narrower retrieval target. The notes' original contents, dates and relationship to the chronology remain unknown.
+
+[Public Commission archive containing item 819 and the Hyde interview file](https://archive.org/download/911datasets/NARA_9-11_Commission_Records_Released_Jan_14_2009.zip) · [Official NARA 00244, p. 1](https://nara-media-001.s3.amazonaws.com/arcmedia/9-11/MFR/t-0148-911MFR-00244.pdf#page=1) · [Previous working-copy comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/2841a9356eb57367a7559c968d65529935f0bedd/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-june4-followup-and-ops-center-copies-2026-11-09/README.md)
+
+## Reading and unresolved inputs
+
+The two Commission PDFs were acquired as exact byte-range ZIP members and checked against the central-directory names, lengths and CRCs. All **16** newly acquired page text layers were screened. Visual review focused on the MFR heading and note-taking paragraph, the relevant Hyde handwritten lines and the two question pages' function. The handwritten pages have sparse extraction, so the report transcribes only the cited fields. Reading scope excludes a full transcript, independent witness verification and clock or sequence reconstruction. [Source pins](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+- [ ] **PD07, DOT source side.** Seek the identified staff timing notes, dated originals and any annotation history in the Office of the Secretary or chief-of-staff files. Check associated routing, copy labels, date and time basis. Treat these as separate from the requested office call logs and the Crisis Management Center AIM event history unless an original record joins them.
+- [ ] **PD01 / PD07, chronology and delivery.** Seek the FAA chronology working copies, final copy and transmitting and receiving entries. Test whether the chief-of-staff timing notes were supplied to FAA or used in any version. Separately seek the operations-center participant log and agency transfer inventories.
+- [ ] **PD01–PD04.** The May 2003 corrected answer, delivery acknowledgment, signed consideration or action/no-action decision and recommendation-specific outcomes remain open. [OIG recommendations 1 and 2, p. 12](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=12) · [Recommendations 3 and 4, p. 13](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=13)
